    "en": {
      "shared_perspectives": "German media, from left-liberal to conservative outlets, consistently stress that the rapid development of large-language models and other AI systems is creating urgent safety and regulatory challenges, prompting calls for stricter oversight, clearer data-protection rules and a more coherent EU AI framework. At the same time, all sides agree that Germany's competitiveness now hinges on a swift expansion of digital infrastructure: broadband, cloud and high-performance computing, and on large-scale upskilling programmes to mitigate the employment disruptions AI is expected to cause. This dual narrative of heightened risk management coupled with a coordinated push for digital capacity building appears across the political spectrum.",
